problems.problem:
a) Show that if $(x_i)$ is a decreasing sequence of positive numbers
then
$\left( \sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i^2 \right)^{1/2}
\le \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{x_i}{\sqrt{i}}.$

b) Show that there is a constant $C$ so that if $(x_i)$ is a decreasing
sequence of positive numbers then
$\sum_{m=1}^{\infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{m}}
\left( \sum_{i=m}^{\infty} x_i^2 \right)^{1/2}
\le C \sum_{i=1}^{\infty} x_i.$

